    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0387" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC Indonesia/9–2548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Batavia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Livengood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Batavia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-09-25T18:00:00+08:00">September 25,
                            1948—6 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>836. Gocus 393. NethDel comments on RepDel report to SC on recent developments in
                    Indonesia of September 9 (Gocus 375<anchor n="1" xml:id="d285-f1"/>) received by
                    GOC on September 24 (Gocus 391<anchor n="2" xml:id="d285-f2"/>). Transmitting
                    letter from NethDel to GOC states:</p>
                <p>[For text of letter and enclosures, see SC, <hi rendition="#italic">3rd yr.,
                        Suppl</hi>. (Dec), page 75.]</p>
                <p>Signed Cochran.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Livengood.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
